            <note corresp="#d369-f2" n="2" xml:id="d369-f2-content">
                <p>Attached but not printed is a June 29 action memorandum from Enders and Blackwill
                    to Haig. On the memorandum, Bremer indicated Haig’s disapproval of the
                    recommendation to forward the attached memorandum to the President seeking
                    authorization to lift economic sanctions and added the following notation:
                    “Secretary signed an alternative memo to the President on the subject.”
                    (Department of State, Central Foreign Policy File, P890076–1218)</p>
            </note>
